 ## Background
-The configurations were introduced in the context of optimizing Sparse Voxel DAGs for efficient geometry representation of voxelized 3D scenes. The study tested three polygonal surface models: Angel Lucy (489k triangles), Porsche (22k triangles), and Skull (80k triangles), voxelized at resolutions from $128^3$ to $4096^3$ [S1]. The goal was to determine the optimal balance between pointer length and addressing word size to minimize binary representation size [S1].
+The SVDAG parameter configurations were introduced to optimize the memory representation of voxelized 3D scenes using Sparse Voxel Directed Acyclic Graphs. The baseline SVO and SVDAG1 configurations follow the layout defined in reference [17] [S1]. The subsequent variants (SVDAG2–SVDAG6) were developed to explore the trade-offs between pointer length, addressing word size, and compression efficiency, leveraging the symmetry-aware node layout of SSVDAG [S1].
 
